# Planted bugs in split_evenly. Each one must make the named command miss its expectation.
run fv-crosshair money.crosshair
properties SplitEvenlyHoldsItsContract RefactorPreservesOutput
file money.py

mutation one share is dropped from the result
detects SplitEvenlyHoldsItsContract
-     return [base + 1 if i < extra else base for i in range(parts)]
+     return [base + 1 if i < extra else base for i in range(parts - 1)]

mutation the extra cents move to the last shares instead of the first, outside the diff
detects RefactorPreservesOutput
-     base, extra = divmod(total, parts)
-     return [base + 1 if i < extra else base for i in range(parts)]
+     base, extra = divmod(total, parts)
+     return [base + 1 if i >= parts - extra else base for i in range(parts)]

harmless a comment is reworded
- """The same split, written as an explicit loop instead of a comprehension."""
+ """The same split, written out as a loop so each cent assignment is a separate step."""
